    <p class="p" style="font-size:20px;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 18px">A site that feels like your brand and makes the next step obvious on every page.</p>
    <a href="/web-development" class="label red">See how we work &rarr;</a>
  </div>
</div></section>
<section data-expansion style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="narrow">
<h2 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(34px,4vw,52px);margin:0 0 28px;max-width:860px">How we design a store that looks like your brand</h2>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">Good design makes a store easy to trust and easy to buy from. It also reflects the business behind it. Many stores look like a template: the same layout, the same stock imagery and the same generic copy as thousands of others. Buyers notice, and it makes the store harder to remember.</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We start by understanding the brand. That means your products, your customers, what you want them to feel, and what you want them to do. We agree those goals with you before any layout is drawn.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">What the design process includes</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 26px;padding-left:22px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--ink2)"><li style="margin:0 0 8px">A brief that sets the goals, the audience and the brand rules.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">Layout sketches for the key pages: home, collection, product and checkout.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">A visual system covering colour, type, spacing and buttons, so every page stays consistent.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">A review with you before anything is built.</li><li style="margin:0 0 8px">Design files and simple rules, so your team can add pages later without breaking the look.</li></ul>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">Platforms</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">We design for Shopify, BigCommerce, WooCommerce, Magento and WordPress. Each platform has its own limits, and the design has to work within them. We'll tell you early if a design idea won't work on your platform, and suggest a version that will.</p>
<p class="label red" style="margin:36px 0 14px">Design for phones first</p>
<p class="p" style="font-size:18px;margin:0 0 22px">Most shopping now happens on phones. We design the mobile layout first, then adapt it for larger screens. That keeps the buying action easy to reach, the text easy to read and the images fast to load.</p>
<h3 class="disp" style="font-size:clamp(32px,3.6vw,44px);margin:56px 0 24px">Frequently asked questions</h3>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--ink);margin:0 0 20px"><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Will you use our existing brand?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Yes. If you have a brand guide, we'll follow it. If you don't, we'll help you set the basics before we design.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Can you redesign one page, or only the whole store?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">Both. Many projects start with the product page, because it has the biggest effect on sales.</p></details><details style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px 0"><summary style="font-size:20px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer">Do you handle copy and photography?</summary><p class="p" style="margin:14px 0 0">We'll advise on both, and we can work with your existing photos. Professional photography is something we can recommend, but it's a separate cost.</p></details></div>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap">
